cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SCS: A Frequency-Domain Wave-Packet Encoding System with a Hardware-Validated Quantum Bridge"
abstract: >-
  SCS (Space Computing System) is a frequency-domain wave-packet encoding
  system in which the carrier frequency carries the payload and the phase carries
  context. This release adds a hardware-validated quantum bridge: the encoding was measured on a real 156-qubit superconducting QPU (IBM
  ibm_marrakesh, 2000 shots per run, 2026-10-06), reaching 99.3% Bell balance on
  two qubits, 98.8% on a reproducibility run, and an ideal three-qubit GHZ
  distribution. The decoding formulas' assumption P(q0=1)=sin^2(theta/2) is
  therefore measurement-verified rather than assumed. The measurement layer, the
  encoding primitives and the reference circuits are hardware-independent and
  depend only on the Python standard library. Classical and hardware proofs are
  reported as strictly separate evidence levels.
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: MIT
